# Internal research/audit docs — local-only, not shipped (see AGENTS.md
# "Internal-docs policy"). Matched by shape, not by an enumerated list of past
# filenames: the previous list named 8 spellings (docs/inspirations*.md,
# inspiration7.md, unsloth_webtools_inspiration.md, ...) and root-level
# inspiration.md / inspirations.md walked straight through it and were
# committed. A gate that enumerates known-bad spellings admits the next one.
*[Ii]nspiration*.md
docs/observability-gaps.md
docs/perf-improvements.md

# Same policy stated the other way round: root-level Markdown is scratch unless
# explicitly shipped, so a new note cannot even be `git add`ed by accident. The
# allow-list lives in scripts/check-tracked-hygiene.mjs (issue #165 F5); speed.md,
# newfeatures.md, implementationplan.md and roadmap_0_5.md all shipped while only
# a name-based blocklist existed.
/*.md
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!ROADMAP.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md

# aio-webresearch bundles are working artifacts, never repo content
# (research-paramtest/ was 14 tracked files).
/research-*/
.pi/webaio-research/

# Ad-hoc root scripts (test-youtube.mjs was tracked this way).
/test-*.mjs

# Generated compile trees from the tla/ verification workflow (tsc --outDir
# tla/compiled...). Never commit these; the checker sources are the artifact.
tla/compiled*/
